Dear Delegate,

Your registration is confirmed for the Youth and AI Summit, commemorating
International Youth Day 2026 at the United Nations Headquarters, New York
City.

*Carefully read the instructions below: *

*Event Details*
Date: 12 August 2026
Venue: Conference Room 4, United Nations Headquarters, New York
Time: 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM, with a break from 1:00 to 3:00 PM
Full agenda: www.iycforyouth.org/iyd2026

Please follow us on Instagram at www.instagram.com/iycforyouth for program
updates in the lead-up to the event.

*Arrival and Pass Pickup*
UN passes and special event tickets can be picked up starting at 8:30 AM on
12 August at the United Nations Visitors' Entrance, 1st Avenue at East 46th
Street, New York, NY. Please note the event is expected to be crowded, so
we encourage you to arrive early to allow time for pass pickup and security
screening before the program begins at 10:00 AM.

*ID Requirements*
All delegates must bring a valid, government-issued photo ID that matches
the name used at registration. This includes a passport, driver's license,
or national ID card. Delegates whose ID does not match their registration
will not be able to collect a pass.

*Speaking on the Floor*
During most sessions, delegates will have the opportunity to make
interventions from the floor. Instructions on how to do so will be provided
by the moderators during each session.

We encourage delegates to prepare their statements in advance, on topics
such as AI governance and policy making, the use of AI in diplomacy, or
anything they would like to see reflected in the Declaration on AI Policy
and Governance. This youth-led Declaration will be carried forward into
ongoing United Nations processes.

*Delegates Under 18*
United Nations security requires that all delegates under 18 be accompanied
by a registered chaperone. This may be a parent, guardian, or a group
chaperone if attending with others.

Chaperones must register using the same registration form as the delegate,
so a pass can be prepared for them.

If a delegate does not have a chaperone, we can arrange for a member of the
IOY team to escort and chaperone them. This IOY chaperone will accompany
the delegate from outside United Nations Headquarters and throughout the
day. This requires signed parental consent.

*Parental Consent Form*
Required for all delegates under 18. Must be signed by a parent or legal
guardian and sent to iyd@iycforyouth.org.

*Deadline*
Registration, chaperone registration, and the parental consent form must
all be completed by 9 August 2026, 11:59 PM EDT.

If you have any questions, please don't hesitate to reach out.

We look forward to welcoming you.




*Warm regards,TeamYouth and AI SummitInternational Organization of Youth*

